abstract: >-
  Investigates the training dynamics of Neural Collapse in Variational
  Quantum Circuits. Shows that a trained VQC collapses only in the
  measurement-visible subspace read by the loss, while the full
  representation's Hilbert-Schmidt geometry is provably and numerically
  (~1e-15 relative change) invariant under training -- collapse is a
  training-driven rotation, not a contraction. Verified to machine
  precision on a synthetic benchmark, real vision data (MNIST,
  Fashion-MNIST), three qubit counts, and two independent IBM hardware
  backends.
keywords:
  - neural collapse
  - variational quantum circuits
  - representation geometry
  - measurement subspace
  - terminal phase of training
  - quantum machine learning
